        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R5 /PWM_OUT PWM 1"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the fan PWM input has an internal pull-up or experiences a fault, the 1 Ω resistor cannot limit current; the PWM line may be held high by the fan, preventing the MCU from pulling it low and possibly causing excessive current or unintended fan behavior.",
